-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",386,{
[12321]="70017512\n1\tReturn the lash to Eilíefr at the Twenty-first Hall\030Collect Igash's lash (quantity: see journal)\tIgash can be found atop the Grand Stair, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall where Eilífr holds his post. Eilífr has asked you to defeat Igash and collect his lash to assist in efforts to reclaim that cross-roads for the dwarves. He wishes to see the lash as proof of your deed.\n",
[12322]="70017511\n1\tReturn the marks to Eilífr at the Twenty-first Hall\030Collect the Devoted's Mark (quantity: see journal)\030Collect the Beast's Mark (quantity: see journal)\030Collect Gothgaash's Mark (quantity: see journal)\030Collect Glothrok's Mark (quantity: see journal)\tMany tribes of Orcs prowl the Grand Stair, their leaders among them, found south-east of the Twenty-first Hall. Eilífr has asked you to defeat Orc leaders in the Grand Stair to assist in efforts to reclaim that cross-roads for the dwarves. He wishes to see their Marks as proof of your deed.\n",
[12323]="7001751F\n1\tKill enemies in the Grand Stair (total: 75)\tMany tribes of Orcs prowl the Grand Stair, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall. Geirr has asked you to defeat many Orcs in the Grand Stair to assist in efforts to reclaim that cross-roads for the dwarves.\n2\tReturn to Geirr at the Twenty-first Hall\tGeirr is in the Twenty-first Hall, north-west of the Grand Stair. Geirr will wish to hear of your success among the Orcs in the once-beautiful cross-roads of the dwarves.\n",
[12324]="7004014C\n1\tTravel to the Tingobel mine\tThe Tingobel mine can be found in the rear of Tingobel to the north of Lancrath. Orodir has asked that you slay the leader of the Orc forces encamped in Tingobel.\n2\tSearch for something valuable to draw forth Ulkfrúm and defeat him\tThe leader of the Rashat-hai Orcs can be found somewhere in the Tingobel mine. You have entered the Tingobel mine, but have not yet found the Orc. You should search for something valuable to draw his attention.\n3\tTalk to Orodir\tOrodir can be found in Lancrath, to the south of Tingobel in Blackroot Vale. You have defeated the Orc-leader, Ulkfrúm, in the Tingobel mine. You should return to Orodir and tell him of the Orc's defeat.\n",
[12325]="700377B4\n1\tPick up the paper in Gladsúnu's hand\tA note lies in Gladsúnu's hand. Gladsúnu's body is at the Fords of Isen. You should collect the note in Gladsúnu's hand.\n2\tRead the letter\tYou have discovered a letter clutched in Gladsúnu's hand. You should read the letter.\n3\tFind Agelwyn at Helm's Deep\tAgelwyn can be found in the Hornburg at Helm's Deep. near the stables and vendors. You should bring Gladsúnu's letter to Agelwyn to notify her of her husband's death.\n",
[12326]="70055057\n1\tDeliver the cracked lances to a collection box\030Collect cracked lances (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire cracked lances.\n",
[12327]="7000834D\n1\tBring the crawler-flesh to Tasgall\030Collect crawler-flesh (total: 8)\tCrawlers can be found in the general area not far north of Aughaire. Hunt crawlers for their flesh and bring it back to Tasgall to be roasted.\n2\tSpeak with Tasgall\tTasgall has roasted the crawlers you brought him. You can return to him to learn the next step in his plan to defeat the Beast-mother.\n3\tUse Great Stone\030Collect Roasted Crawler-flesh\030Defeat Bangrath\tThe rock in the hill-beast lair is at the entrance to the valley, not far north of Aughaire. Tasgall has given you some roasted crawler-flesh, which you should bring to a certain rock in the lairs of the hill-beasts.\n4\tSpeak with Tasgall\tHaving successfully defeated the Beast-mother, you should return to Tasgall's camp and speak with him.\n5\tSpeak with Tasgall\tYou have defeated the vengeful Beast-lord and saved Tasgall's life. Speak with him.\n",
[12328]="7005298C\n1\tGather wheat (total: 6)\030Collect seeds (total: 10)\030Gather honey (total: 4)\tWild wheat and seeds can be found north and east of the Beorninghús. You should collect wheat and seeds for your honey cake.\n2\tUse the mortar and pestle at the Beorninghús to crush the wheat and seeds\tA mortar and pestle can be found at the Beorninghús. You should crush the wheat and seeds that you have collected.\n3\tAdd the honey to the mixture\tThe mortar and pestle can be found at the Beorninghús. You should add the honey to the mixture you have made.\n4\tBake your batter in the oven\tThe oven can be found at the Beorninghús. You should put your cake in the oven.\n5\tWait and watch your cake\tThe oven can be found at the Beorninghús. You should wait by the oven for your cake to bake.\n6\tTake your honey cake out of the oven\tThe oven can be found at the Beorninghús. You should take your cake out of the oven.\n7\tPresent your perfect honey cake inside Grimbeorn's lodge\tA cake stand can be found inside Grimbeorn's lodge. You should present your cake on the stand.\n8\tShow Hállkell your perfect honey cake\tHállkell can be found at the Beorninghús. You should show your perfect honey cake to Hállkell.\n",
[12329]="7000C381\n1\tSpeak with Aeglas\tAeglas must be protected as he attempts to lead Glorwen and Oghûk to safety. It falls to you to defend him along the way.\n2\tTalk to Glóin at his camp outside of Goblin-town\tGlóin is just outside the entrance to Goblin-town. With your aid, Aeglas and Glorwen escaped to safety. Oghûk proved as treacherous as any goblin. You should report your victories to Glóin.\n",
[12330]="70032BEE\n1\tListen to Dómárr's tale\tReinn can be found in the Great Hall of Durin. You should speak with Reinn.\n2\tSpeak with Dómárr\tDómárr can be found in the Great Hall of Durin. You should speak with Dómárr.\n",
[12331]="7002274E\n1\tMay Gamgee became separated from her friends inside the Haunted Burrow, as they disappeared from her side one-by-one. You should seek May's friends and nudge them towards the door.\t\n2\tReturn to May Gamgee with news of her friends\tMay Gamgee is outside the Haunted Burrow, near the Party Tree. You should return to May Gamgee with news that all of her friends are quite well.\n",
[12332]="70046106\n1\tSpeak with Melia Pott to begin\tThe pond is north of Bywater. Billard Pott has told you of an amazing opportunity to fish up mathoms from the Bywater pond.\n2\tHook as many mathoms as you can before time runs out\tThe pond is north of Bywater. Billard Pott has told you of an amazing opportunity to fish up mathoms from the Bywater pond.\n",
[12333]="7005AB0C\n1\tExamine the statue of The First Great Moot\030Examine the statue of The Second Great Moot\030Examine the statue of The Third Great Moot\030Examine the statue of The Fourth Great Moot\030Examine the statue of The Fifth Great Moot\030Examine the statue of The Sixth Great Moot\030Examine the statue of The Seventh Great Moot\tSeven statues representing the Great Moots can be found in Ibdêkh-buzru, the Thing-fold. You should examine the statues.\n2\tTalk to Kyrstig\tKyrstig can be found just outside Ibdêkh-buzru, the Thing-fold. You should talk to Kyrstig.\n",
[12334]="7005B000\n1\tDefeat Orcs at Azanulbizar (total: 30)\tOrcs can be found throughout Azanulbizar. King Thráin has asked you to slay Orcs at Azanulbizar.\n2\tTalk to King Thráin at Amdân\tKing Thráin can be found at Amdân. You have slain many of the Orcs at Azanulbizar. You should talk to King Thráin.\n",
[12335]="70044EB6\n1\tTravel to Minas Tirith\tThis may be a wonderful time to explore Middle-earth.\n2\tTake flight off the prow of Minas Tirith\tMinas Tirith is a lovely place.\n3\tLand!\tThis may be a wonderful time to explore Middle-earth.\n",
[12336]="70044EB7\n1\tExamine George\tYou think that perhaps it is time to escape Farmer Sandson's coop.\n",
[12337]="70054685\n1\tDefeat gredbyg in Torech Ungol (total: 10)\tMany gredbyg have responded to the call of Shelob and taken up residence in her lair. You should defeat gredbyg inside Torech Ungol.\n2\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas is standing by outside Torech Ungol. You should talk to Legolas.\n",
[12338]="7000E8B6\n1\tDefeat Gurmagath\tThe Stone-troll chieftain Gurmagath is in the forests south-east of Dol Nendír. Handarod has asked you to find Gurmagath and defeat him. He suggested that you take allies with you.\n2\tTalk to Handarod\tHandarod is in Esteldín, north of Dol Nendir. You should return to Handarod and tell him of Gurmagath's defeat.\n",
[12339]="70019060\n1\tSearch the maze for an Inn League artifact\tThe hedge maze is in the Horse-fields, to the north of Bree-town. It seems as though Tob Sandyman just gave you a challenge, but it's not quite clear what it was. You should explore the centre of the maze for a clue that might clarify what this Inn League member has planned for you. NOTE: This quest will fail if you log out of the game prior to completion and turn-in.\n2\tFind the exit before the time runs out\tThe maze exit seems to be leagues and leagues away from where you now stand. If you can manage to walk at all, you should make your way out of the maze before the time runs out. NOTE: This quest will fail when logging out of the game. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Tob Sandyman\tTob Sandyman is outside the hedge-maze on the Horse-fields in Bree. You should speak with Tob and find out exactly why you went into the hedge maze to begin with. NOTE: This quest will fail when logging out of the game.\n",
[12340]="70000013\n1\tBring the barrel back to Barmy Rootknot\030Collect the dwarf-barrel\tThe lost barrel is somewhere north-west of Overhill. The Green Dragon Inn is in Bywater, south-east of Overhill. Barmy Rootknot, the assistant innkeeper at The Green Dragon Inn, has sent you off in search of a lost brandy-barrel.\n",
[12341]="70052948\n1\tBlómgard can be found at the edge of the southern wood of Laerlad in the Vales of Anduin. You should listen to the stories of the Woodmen of Blómgard.\t\n2\tBlómgard can be found at the edge of the southern wood of Laerlad in the Vales of Anduin. You should offer words of encouragement to the Woodmen of Blómgard.\t\n3\tTalk to Odahild\tOdahild can be found in Blómgard. You should talk to Odahild, the leader of Blómgard.\n",
[12342]="700621CF\n1\tDefeat Greenway raiders (total: 4)\030Defeat Greenway knaves (total: 4)\030Defeat Greenway bowmen (total: 4)\tGerwyn has asked you to defeat bandits who chased them out of Andrath. The bandits are south of Andrath, in northern Cardolan.\n2\tReturn to Gerwyn\tYou should tell Gerwyn that you defeated a number of Greenway bandits. Gerwyn is in the circle of caravans, in northern Cardolan.\n",
[12343]="70020DA6\n1\tFind and defeat the Grey King\tThe entrance to the Grey King's lair lies in a gully to the south-west of Maur Tulhau. Iolo Brochtû has asked you to rid his village of the threat of the Grey King.\n2\tTalk to Iolo Brochtû at Maur Tulhau\tIolo Brochtû is at Maur Tulhau, north-east of the Grey King's lair. You should return to Iolo Brochtû with news of the Grey King's defeat.\n",
[12344]="7004F91A\n1\tLook into the Grey Wrack from Stánbalk, the Stone Wall\030Scale the ruins of Stánbalk, the Stone Wall\tStánbalk, the Stone Wall can be found to the south of Thikil-gundu. Dori has asked you to scale Stánbalk, the Stone Wall and scout for nearby foes.\n2\tTalk to Dori on the road to Thikil-gundu\tDori can be found on a hilltop overlooking Stánbalk, the Stone Wall of Thikil-gundu. You have scaled Stánbalk, the Stone Wall, and you have found it empty of foes. You should now speak to Dori.\n3\tTalk to Dori atop Stánbalk, the Stone Wall\tDori can be found atop Stánbalk, the Stone Wall. Dori and Company have made camp atop Stánbalk, the Stone Wall. You should now speak to Dori.\n4\tSearch the Grey Wrack for signs of Nori's expedition\tThe Grey Wrack lies between Stánbalk, the Stone Wall and Thikil-gundu. Dori has asked you to search the Grey Wrack for signs of Nori and his expedition.\n5\tTalk to Ingór, son of Vékun in the Grey Wrack\tIngór, son of Vékun can be found in the Grey Wrack. You have found Ingór, son of Vékun while searching the Grey Wrack, but he appears to be wounded. You should speak to Ingór, son of Vékun.\n6\tBurn slain Longbeards and Zhélruka in the Grey Wrack ([see journal]/12)\030Burn the remains of dwarf-wights (total: 8)\tSlain dwarves and dwarf-wights can be found throughout the Grey Wrack. Fearing that none of their bodies can be recovered, Ingór, son of Vékun has asked you to burn the remains of his fallen companions as well as the remains of the terrible dwarf-wights that wander the Grey Wrack.\n7\tSearch for Nori before the gates of Thikil-gundu\tThikil-gundu can be found beyond the Grey Wrack. You have made your way to Thikil-gundu and should now search for some sign of Nori and his expedition.\n8\tReclaim Nori's axe before the gates of Thikil-gundu\tNori's axe can be found outside the gates of Thikil-gundu. You have discovered Nori's axe amid a pile of Karazgar's rust. You should collect Nori's axe.\n9\tDeliver Nori's axe to Dori atop Stánbalk, the Stone Wall\tDori can be found atop Stánbalk, the Stone Wall. You have found Nori's axe amid a pile of Karazgar's rust. You should return to Dori at once.\n",
[12345]="700544D3\n1\tDefeat the Grim Southron in Mordor Besieged\tFew among the living ever heard him speak, but his visage was well-known, and feared. They called him the Grim Southron, and while Men quailed at his approach during the Second Age, during the Third the legend of his malice had only grown. In later days it was he that Lhaereth the Stained followed in secret to Dol Guldur, where she discovered Sauron and helped him recover, for a price. Did the Dark Lord deal out reward or punishment for his Nazgûl's lapse? But that was much later. During the Second Age, the Grim Southron was known only to be patient, loyal, and silent.\n2\tDefeat the Grim Southron in Mordor Besieged\tFew among the living ever heard him speak, but his visage was well-known, and feared. They called him the Grim Southron, and while Men quailed at his approach during the Second Age, during the Third the legend of his malice had only grown. In later days it was he that Lhaereth the Stained followed in secret to Dol Guldur, where she discovered Sauron and helped him recover, for a price. Did the Dark Lord deal out reward or punishment for his Nazgûl's lapse? But that was much later. During the Second Age, the Grim Southron was known only to be patient, loyal, and silent.\n3\tThe Grim Southron, defeated but enduring\tFew among the living ever heard him speak, but his visage was well-known, and feared. They called him the Grim Southron, and while Men quailed at his approach during the Second Age, during the Third the legend of his malice had only grown. In later days it was he that Lhaereth the Stained followed in secret to Dol Guldur, where she discovered Sauron and helped him recover, for a price. Did the Dark Lord deal out reward or punishment for his Nazgûl's lapse? But that was much later. During the Second Age, the Grim Southron was known only to be patient, loyal, and silent.\n",
[12346]="70053E34\n1\tExamine the Orc corpse on the road to Minas Morgul\030Defeat Morgul sentries (total: 5)\tOrc sentries and corpses can be found in Rath Dúath. You should defeat Orc sentries and examine any Orc corpses that you find.\n2\tSeek out another Orc corpse in Rath Dúath\tAnother Orc corpse can be found closer to Echad Uial in Rath Dúath. You should seek out another Orc corpse to examine.\n3\tFind the creature that is attacking Orcs\tFootprints can be found leading away from the Orc corpse. You should follow the footprints.\n4\tTalk to Thurindol at Echad Uial\tThurindol can be found at Echad Uial in Rath Dúath. You should talk to Thurindol.\n",
[12347]="70046C27\n1\tDefeat Orcs and Easterlings in North Ithilien (total: 20)\tOrcs and Easterlings can be found throughout North Ithilien. Orcs and Easterlings pose a grave threat to the Rangers of Ithilien and the Host of the West. You should defeat them to aid in the protection of Gondor's lands.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many Orcs and Easterlings in North Ithilien.\n",
[12348]="70062FD8\n1\tDefeat Uruk-hai warriors (total: 12)\030Defeat Uruk-hai archers (total: 8)\030Defeat Uruk-hai captains (total: 2)\tMayor Eirlys Dringarth has asked you to defeat foes at Sharmokal. Sharmokal is in southern Swanfleet.\n2\tReturn to Mayor Dringarth\tYou should let Eirlys Dringarth know that you have defeated many foes at Sharmokal. Eirlys is in Lintrev.\n",
[12349]="70052965\n1\tCordially bow to Landroval\tLandroval can be found at the Eyrie. You should be polite to Landroval.\n2\tTalk to Landroval\tLandroval can be found at the Eyrie. You should talk to Landroval.\n3\tCordially bow to Meneldor\tMeneldor can be found at the Eyrie. You should be polite to Meneldor.\n4\tTalk to Meneldor\tMeneldor can be found at the Eyrie. You should talk to Meneldor.\n5\tLook at the lands to the north\030Look at the lands to the east\030Look at the lands to the south\tThe Eyrie can be reached from the Carrock in the Beorning-lands. You should look out over the Eyrie at the lands below.\n6\tTalk to Gwaihir the Wind-lord\tGwaihir the Wind-lord can be found at the Eyrie. You should talk to Gwaihir.\n",
[12350]="7003A49E\n1\tObserve Gríma reprimanding the White Hand leaders\tYou once again encounter Gríma Wormtongue, this time reprimanding the leaders of Madh-fushaum for what appear to be failures on their part. He clearly had business to attend to here before departing for Isengard.\n2\tObserve Gríma reprimanding the White Hand leaders\tYou should observe Gríma reprimanding the leaders of Madh-fushaum for what appears to be failures on their part. You may be able to learn what involvement he has in the situation in the Stonedeans.\n3\tObserve Gríma reprimanding the White Hand leaders\tGríma has finished his business in Madh-fushaum and now departs for Isengard.\n4\tTalk with Herubrand\tWhat you observed of Gríma Wormtongue's business with the leaders of Madh-fushaum and the role he has played in the Stonedean's turmoil would be wise to share with Herubrand.\n",
[12351]="700559A4\n1\tDefeat Ongûl\tOngûl can be found at Thoremband upon the Circle of Death. You should defeat Ongûl.\n2\tDefeat Ongûl\tOngûl can be found at Thoremband upon the Circle of Death. You should defeat Ongûl.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated Ongûl.\n",
[12352]="70049266\n1\tDefeat Barad-dûr sentries (total: 8)\tBarad-dûr sentries can be found near the bones of Barad-dûr. You should defeat an sentries that you come across.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeat many Barad-dûr sentries.\n",
})
